0..77 Comment "// What a domhringr stage performs besides its session\'s moves, each effect a"
78..153 Comment "// theory of its operations with its first-order laws. A session\'s protocol"
154..224 Comment "// stays a session type: the ordered, linear channel is not an effect."
225..227 Comment "//"
228..303 Comment "// Each theory\'s documentation states what it commutes with. Every row is a"
304..380 Comment "// set whatever commutes; the commutation table decides which operations the"
381..455 Comment "// fusion pass may reorder. A commutation past an operation that answers a"
456..531 Comment "// value is a law over continuations, each operation taking what runs after"
532..608 Comment "// it and `bind x . …` binding the value it answers; those laws follow the"
609..684 Comment "// effects, one theory per law. An effect commuting with nothing has no law"
685..697 Comment "// to write."
698..700 Comment "//"
701..772 Comment "// The instance an effect is performed at (a store, a task\'s journal, a"
773..834 Comment "// sink) is the label a row names it by, not a second theory."
836..910 Comment "/// The record plane\'s content-addressed values: a put answers the value\'s"
911..986 Comment "/// digest, and the digest gets the value back. A put is idempotent, so the"
987..1038 Comment "/// store commutes with every effect. One instance."
